There's no project code in this directory, so this assumes TypeScript and an existing `getUserProfile(userId)` fetcher; swap in your names.

```ts
const TTL_MS = 60_000;
const cache = new Map<string, { value: Promise<UserProfile>; expires: number }>();

export function getUserProfileCached(userId: string): Promise<UserProfile> {
  const hit = cache.get(userId);
  if (hit && hit.expires > Date.now()) return hit.value;

  // Cache the promise so concurrent requests share one fetch.
  const value = getUserProfile(userId);
  cache.set(userId, { value, expires: Date.now() + TTL_MS });
  // Do not keep failed fetches.
  value.catch(() => cache.delete(userId));
  return value;
}

// Call this from every code path that updates a profile.
export function invalidateUserProfile(userId: string): void {
  cache.delete(userId);
}
```

Security warning: this keys on `userId` alone, so it is only safe if the response is identical for every viewer. If the profile includes fields that depend on who is asking, add the viewer's ID to the key.

I left out eviction, so the map grows with every distinct user until restart; add a size cap or an LRU if you serve many users. It is also per-process, so with more than one server instance invalidation will not reach the others, and you would move it to Redis.
